    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find out how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the amount Steven pays per room by the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Identify the amount Steven pays per room: $\\frac{11}{2}$ dollars.\n2. Identify the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned: $\\frac{7}{3}$ rooms.\n3. Multiply the two quantities together:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{2} \\times \\frac{7}{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. To multiply these fractions, multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11 \\times 7}{2 \\times 3} = \\frac{77}{6}\n   \\]\n\nSo, Steven owes Jeremy \\(\\frac{77}{6}\\) dollars. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{77}{6}}\n\\]",
