    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine how much Steven owes Jeremy, we need to multiply the number of rooms Jeremy cleaned by the amount Steven pays per room. The calculation is as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total payment} = \\text{Number of rooms} \\times \\text{Payment per room}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of rooms} = \\frac{7}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Payment per room} = \\frac{11}{2}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total payment} = \\frac{7}{3} \\times \\frac{11}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we multiply the numerators:\n\n\\[\n7 \\times 11 = 77\n\\]\n\nThen, we multiply the denominators:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 2 = 6\n\\]\n\nSo, the total payment is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total payment} = \\frac{77}{6}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Steven owes Jeremy \\(\\boxed{\\frac{77}{6}}\\) dollars.",
